00:06:47.028 --> 00:06:51.948
The policy analysis market is a proposal for contracts on political and security events,

00:06:51.948 --> 00:06:56.668
And the way it works is that the list of questions can fail before any price is tested.

00:06:57.268 --> 00:07:01.008
A yes position pays only if someone later judges that the event occurred.

00:07:01.648 --> 00:07:04.748
A no position pays only if that judgment goes the other way.

00:07:05.368 --> 00:07:07.808
Call she caps a contract's payout at $1.

00:07:08.188 --> 00:07:10.248
So the price is a slice of that dollar.

00:07:10.848 --> 00:07:12.688
Arithmetic does not pick the question.

00:07:13.268 --> 00:07:16.028
A venue does, or a regulator, or a public storm.

00:07:16.708 --> 00:07:18.368
Aggregation is the design claim.

00:07:18.368 --> 00:07:24.048
A person who will never send a memo can still buy or sell and each trade nudges the number.

00:07:24.528 --> 00:07:29.068
If the wording is tight and the crowd is not one trader wearing many hats, scattered

00:07:29.068 --> 00:07:31.048
views get pressed into a single figure.

00:07:31.648 --> 00:07:33.468
The fight starts when the question is harmed.

00:07:34.068 --> 00:07:38.628
Getting paid for correctly calling a violent or destabilizing event gives someone a cash

00:07:38.628 --> 00:07:40.268
reason to be right about damage.

00:07:40.908 --> 00:07:42.048
Critics hear a bounty.

00:07:42.648 --> 00:07:45.628
People who want the listing say a ban does not erase the views.

00:07:45.628 --> 00:07:49.468
It only keeps them off a screen where price and size can be seen.

00:07:49.988 --> 00:07:53.368
Stay with that $1 cap and do not borrow a live quote.

00:07:53.848 --> 00:07:58.128
Whatever fraction a yes buyer puts up is the loss if the contract resolves no.

00:07:58.728 --> 00:08:02.208
And the unpaid remainder of the dollar is the profit if it resolves yes.

00:08:02.888 --> 00:08:05.188
The other side of the same dollar is the no buyer.

00:08:05.788 --> 00:08:07.268
Concern is not what gets paid.

00:08:07.968 --> 00:08:09.588
Citizenship is not what gets paid.

00:08:10.048 --> 00:08:11.628
A match with the resolution is.

00:08:11.628 --> 00:08:16.948
A designer can therefore call the figure a forecast, an opponent can call it indecent

00:08:16.948 --> 00:08:20.668
the moment the question is an attack, a coup, or some other harm.

00:08:21.208 --> 00:08:25.688
Those are two descriptions of one object, the payout rule, and the sound of the question

00:08:25.688 --> 00:08:26.368
read aloud.

00:08:26.948 --> 00:08:28.608
Other breaks sit next to that rule.

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:33.068
Guessers can still print a number, a few large orders can still shove it.

00:08:33.468 --> 00:08:37.408
A fuzzy resolution rule pays the side that wins the argument about the rule.

00:08:37.408 --> 00:08:42.048
Pull the market when the questions hit the public and there are no settled contracts left

00:08:42.048 --> 00:08:44.928
to score, so hits and misses never get counted.

00:08:45.448 --> 00:08:46.648
That ending is political.

00:08:47.008 --> 00:08:49.268
One side can say the forecast was never tried.

00:08:49.868 --> 00:08:52.268
The other can say the question should never have been sold.

00:08:52.868 --> 00:08:54.808
Neither side can hand a listener a price.

00:08:55.448 --> 00:08:58.848
A figure on a screen is what people who can reach that venue will pay.

00:08:59.388 --> 00:09:02.108
For that question, under that rule, at that moment.

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:07.028
It is not a headcount of everyone who knows something, and it is not a moral verdict.

00:09:07.588 --> 00:09:12.348
A question that never gets listed does not sit at zero, it has no probability attached.

00:09:12.848 --> 00:09:15.048
That is the limit this proposal still teaches.

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:20.608
A price can sum up a trade, and it cannot outlast a decision that the question may not be sold.

